      "created_at": "2018-10-08T14:28:11Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-08T14:28:11Z",
      "body": "There are indeed requests made to Facebook and to Pinterest when you have those 2 non-official sharing buttons on a page. Those are the only 2 services that get requested at the moment. As you mentioned, that can be stopped with a filter, `jetpack_sharing_counts`.\r\n\r\nThe visitor's IP address is not directly sent to each service; only the post URL is. It may, however, appear in Facebook's or Pinterest's access logs as the IP address making the request.\r\n\r\n@pesieminski What is your take on this? Should we add this to the privacy policy helper?\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
