      "created_at": "2018-10-16T09:10:25Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-10-16T09:10:37Z",
      "body": ">  It may, however, appear in Facebook's or Pinterest's access logs as the IP address making the request.\r\n\r\nIANAL, but to the best of my knowledge, submitting IP addresses to third party and storing them in their access logs is exactly something, the GDPR is supposed to prevent. This is not a matter of \"enhancement\" but a (legal) bug, which needs to be fixed if you want Jetpack to comply with GDPR.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
